Turn this into an image, by reading the image we.png
and comparing the visual layout you see in the image
with your knowledge of the exact Unicode characters
I used in the text below, based on your total sum of
knowledge of what it is and what's going on in the
2-dimensional monospaced relationships between the
chatacters and their neighbors w.r.t. spatial proximity
and which letters derived from which others historically
or share similarities of shape or sound.

You must pay attention to the exact unicode characters
I used here in the text. You MUST keep it monospaced,
and be religious about the spacing differences between
CJK characters and the rest, knowing that there is
information running both horizontally and vertically,
through similarities of sound, shape, the history of
writing, puns available only in adjads and especially
in defectively spelled orthographies like the older
strata of Classical Biblical Hebrew.

Do all that now, and make it perfect.

